From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: haroldxie <xiewenhao2308@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: kjit: export the hook's SRCU callback queue for the
 runtime

The KJIT runtime frees translated fragments, and the dispatch tables that
point into them, only after every hook call that could still be running
them has returned. Every execution of translated code happens inside one
kjit_call_after_syscall(), under kjit_hook_srcu, so "a grace period of
that SRCU after the object was retired" is the whole condition. Until now
the runtime approximated it with a reference count taken per run, which
cannot cover a run that continues into a fragment it never looked up.

Export two entry points on the hook's own SRCU, whose srcu_struct stays
private to this file:

  kjit_hook_call_srcu(head, cb)   call_srcu(): runs cb after a grace
                                  period; legal wherever a spinlock may be
                                  taken, so the runtime can retire a
                                  fragment from its mmu_notifier callback
  kjit_hook_srcu_barrier()        srcu_barrier(): waits for every queued
                                  callback, for the runtime's module exit,
                                  which must not leave a callback pointing
                                  into freed module text

Nothing else changes: no new lock, no new state, and the unregister
sequence of the previous patch is untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/kjit.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/kjit.h     |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/kjit.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/kjit.c
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/kjit.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/kjit.c
@@ -85,6 +85,35 @@
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(kjit_unregister_hook);
 
+/**
+ * kjit_hook_call_srcu - run @cb after a grace period of the hook's SRCU
+ * @head: rcu_head embedded in the object @cb frees or unlinks
+ * @cb: called, in a workqueue context with bottom halves disabled, once every
+ *	after_syscall call and extable search that was in flight when this was
+ *	called has returned
+ *
+ * Every execution of translated code happens inside such a call, so an object
+ * a running fragment may still reach (a fragment, its dispatch tables) can be
+ * retired, then freed from @cb. Like call_srcu() it may be called from any
+ * context that may take a spinlock, including with one held.
+ */
+void kjit_hook_call_srcu(struct rcu_head *head, rcu_callback_t cb)
+{
+	call_srcu(&kjit_hook_srcu, head, cb);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(kjit_hook_call_srcu);
+
+/*
+ * Returns once every callback queued with kjit_hook_call_srcu() has run. For
+ * the runtime's exit path, after kjit_unregister_hook() and after it stopped
+ * queueing: nothing of the runtime's may be called after the module is gone.
+ */
+void kjit_hook_srcu_barrier(void)
+{
+	srcu_barrier(&kjit_hook_srcu);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(kjit_hook_srcu_barrier);
+
 long kjit_call_after_syscall(struct pt_regs *regs)
 {
 	const struct kjit_hook_ops *ops;
diff --git a/include/linux/kjit.h b/include/linux/kjit.h
--- a/include/linux/kjit.h
+++ b/include/linux/kjit.h
@@ -61,6 +61,8 @@
 
 int kjit_register_hook(const struct kjit_hook_ops *ops);
 void kjit_unregister_hook(const struct kjit_hook_ops *ops);
+void kjit_hook_call_srcu(struct rcu_head *head, rcu_callback_t cb);
+void kjit_hook_srcu_barrier(void);
 long kjit_call_after_syscall(struct pt_regs *regs);
 int kjit_queue_task_work(struct kjit_task_work *work);
 const struct exception_table_entry *search_kjit_extables(unsigned long addr);
-- 
